        // Since msg.value is 0 but baseToken is address(0), it will proceed to the else branch where it expects msg.value >= netInputAmount
        // For the bug, msg.value == 0, netInputAmount > 0, so it reverts with InvalidEthAmount
        // For reference, baseToken != address(0), msg.value == 0, so it calls ERC20.safeTransferFrom which succeeds

